{"kind":"propose","text":"O2 needs a bounded local record of the exact timed transition across eviction. The existing post-seal callback can miss a committed timer if the object stops before it runs. I propose recording a private outbox receipt in the same transaction that seals the recognized timed entry, keyed to the exact pending send and containing its local sequence, hash, item, rule, and due point. This prices only cutoffs the declaration recognizes and uses indexed reads. The ordinary diagnosis, replay, and late-result path stay on their existing forms. To prove the target, use an internal read-only exact-target RPC over the existing native birth and pinned-definition capture. The current native birth reply omits the declared level. The new reply would report the checked level from that same capture and would leave target delivery state alone. Please flag any objection to these runtime seams while the recognizer is drafted.","body":{"to":"planner"}}